<header><p class="st-kicker">princely state · Indian princely states</p><h1 class="st-title">Tharoch State</h1><p class="st-meta">1500 CE – 1948 CE (approx.) · capital Tharoch</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A small Rajput hill state in the upper Pabbar region east of Shimla, one of the minor Simla Hill States.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Tradition dates the ruling family to around 1500, but little is reliably known of its origins.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Tharoch was a small mountain state related to its neighbour <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/jubbal-state">Jubbal State</a>. It was occupied by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gurkhas">Gurkhas</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-nepal">Kingdom of Nepal</a> in the early 19th century and restored as a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/simla-hill-states">Simla Hill State</a> under British protection after 1815. Its history is poorly recorded.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Tharoch merged into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/himachal-pradesh">Himachal Pradesh</a> in April 1948 and is now part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shimla">Shimla</a> district.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="princely state, 1500 CE – 1948 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">princely state</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Indian princely states</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:89.55%;width:8.92%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1500 CE – 1948 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>princely state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Tharoch</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Hinduism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Western Pahari</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/india">India</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Tharoch</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1724&amp;focus=tharoch-state" aria-label="Tharoch State on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6836 1372 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Tharoch State lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7364 1601h0M7364 1602h0M7018 1386h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7156 1628h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M7156 1628h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day India. <a href="/atlas?year=1724&amp;focus=tharoch-state">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
